From 20c907f3daa5471d2a53ae660f8f5445c727cbfc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 07:00:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(guard): contain state scan regressions by reverting
 PR3001 and PR3537 [daveey]

Revert PR3001's three commits (b9cec91e75, 0bd2abac8b, fb146e85f2)
and PR3537's four commits (786aa9faf2, 3b0a387343, c770147e0d,
d105dfdc9d). Preserve PR3445's Bash 3.2 changes in surviving tests;
its generated-script test disappears with the reverted feature.

This is containment, not a provenance repair. It temporarily restores the
pre-PR3001 generated-file policy, removing unknown-writer execution
refusal. It also restores pre-PR3537 computed-executable fail-opens,
including ${x:-hermes} gateway restart and $(echo hermes) gateway restart.
Existing direct lifecycle, file and budget checks remain; do not claim
this preserves the reverted protections. The orchestrator authorized
both reverts on t_cf2940f30c6b27b1 after the same-state A/B proof.

PR3001 promotes inert destination quote fragments to executed scripts
when an unrelated sink appears. Two added harmless real-Bash controls
fail before containment and pass afterward. PR3537's normalized-command
recursion rescans the entire 1628-line core-wt script, exhausting the
16384-line budget. A diagnostic-only omission of that rescan reveals
an additional unresolved-computed-executable refusal. No diagnostic
bypass is included here.

Same-state acceptance: original published containment 5bef2071b7 passes
2/2; rebase 51522adbf5 fails deliver on line budget (restart control
passes); adding the PR3537 revert restores 2/2 in 20.724 seconds.
The previous full corpus can pass despite the state consumer failure:
305 files, 13652 passed, 9 skipped on the rebased PR3001-only revert.
Full final corpus and exact-head CI/review remain mandatory before land.

Rejected PR3565 must not land. Re-land evidence stays as one note on the
existing lifecycle area card: attachment92, sibling safety tests at
812e48592fab37d79a400c59020597044c2f766b, review t_095726d4610bf4ab,
and the two inert-destination controls. No new guard card or promise
of an automatic re-land; David can request restoration with a safe fix.
